          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On September 27, 1978, at approximately 7:35 PM, a telephone call to the Sète semaphore reported two stationary bright lights in the sky. The on-duty military personnel confirmed the observation and the presence of a first object with a cylindrical shape, a conical and shiny front part, and a second object resembling a crescent that appeared and disappeared. The post commander was contacted and also confirmed the presence of the two objects. The objects disappeared around 8:20 PM behind clouds. These individuals likely observed balloons.",
